    "tree_id": "170fc0447b222cf3422ae896bed1bbf201250956",
    "message": "Reduce live answer preparation and qwen-flash first-token overhead\n\nBuild hash vectors lazily and skip both hash work and semantic waiting on the\nfast formal path. Retain exact completed prefetches, isolate their retrieval\nprofiles, preserve current questions and factual evidence, and bound default\noral history. Overlap screenshots with local context preparation.\n\nSend supported qwen-flash thinking controls on official DashScope, disable\nhidden SDK retries for fast live requests, and record privacy-safe phase\ntimings through first paint. Include reproducible offline benchmarks and a\nfast retrieval comparison.\n\nValidation: 518/519 tests passed; the pre-existing Whisper bundling assertion\nstill fails. Electron UI smoke and 24 focused checks passed. Synthetic RAG\nevaluation preserved candidate recall across 60 cases and 18 SDK replay steps\nhad no cross-project leaks. Same-host 4,000-source preparation improved from\n1060.68ms to 362.39ms cold, and 127.05ms to 29.19ms warm. Real qwen-flash TTFT\nand the user's Windows end-to-end delay were not measured in this Linux task.",
